{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1177290-would-this-be-an-ok-slasher","id":1177290,"title":"Would this be an ok Slasher?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-19T08:06:04-08:00","id":1177290,"title":"Would this be an ok Slasher?","content":"This is my character that I use in a lot of settings &quot;Austin Will&quot;, and I was wondering if he would fit as a Slasher and for that matter just in CofD in general. I don't actually have the Slasher chronicle, i have all the 2e books but none of the 1e ones, but i was wondering what people thought and what type of slasher would they be (or if they don't think he works in CofD or even if he should be something else).<br /> <br /> Bio: a very... creative serial killer, though not exactly the master of subtly. As in just actively tells people he\u2019s a serial killer if they ask. He tends to be quiet and really creepy most of the time, but actually gets really quite social if you talk to him when he\u2019s killing someone or right after. His kills are usually full of vigor and enjoyment, but not sloppied by anger. They tend to be elaborate and creative, though he\u2019s not opposed to something very basic, usually his knife, though he occasionally to uses his bare hands or just a gun if he gets his hands on one. He\u2019s highly trained in most types of killings, as well as a whole bunch of just other skills he uses for setting up kills.<br /> <br /> Backstory: as he began as a young boy on the streets, Austin became a thief to make ends meet, but after killing someone in a theft gone wrong, he felt he loved it. He became better and better at killing, to the point that it was obvious that these kills were done by a master. He mostly survives (of moderate wealth surprisingly) off of whoever he kills, stealing their money as collateral. He doesn\u2019t really care who he kills, he just likes the thrill of it all<br /> <br /> General Facts about the way i play him i didn't mention in either of those:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is sane in a weird sort of way. Not sane like what people mean by like \u201cgone sane\u201d but like. Sane like a person is sane. Pretty much every incarnation of him is basically completely sane except for his killing business (which is of course a pretty big caveat).</li> <li>Is creative and quick to learn new skills, which he usually uses to kill people in new and interesting ways, that usually reference the person killed in some way, and usually are very carefully done.</li> <li>Always speaks in a distinct slow monotone, unless he has recently killed, is killing, or is on something (he would never willingly have drugs mind, but it is an exception)</li> <li>Always leaves his name (\u201cAustin\u201d) somewhere after he killed someone in the crime scenes he leaves</li> <li>Tends to be very clever about not getting caught, while he will admit that is a serial killer if asked, but won't mention unless it directly comes up, and sometimes when it does</li> <li>Is clever about who he kills, and doesn't typically kill people that help him or he just likes as a person generally.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:14:39-08:00","id":1177351,"title":"","content":"As a player character or as an antagonist? <br /> <br /> It's a good start but as far as the backstory goes, besides the juvenile killing, its pretty vanilla. <br /> <br /> Compared to rl examples, Austin as an adult is fairly generic. Serial killers are by a significant majority found to have been involved in petty crimes in their youth (thief), be socially stunted or underdeveloped (quiet and creepy), have a history of familial abuse or negligence (life on the streets), generally reported killing for ecstatic pleasure (loved it, creative outlet), considered generally normal seeming outside of their murderous tendencies (sane outside of killing, doesnt kill people he likes or who helped ), and generally of average or below average intellect, though they think themselves clever (writes his name and freely admits serial killing). <br /> <br /> In the end, these actual serial killer profiles either have a large body count over a very short window (and stop either by being caught, killed, or simply stop due to a temporary state), have a low body count over a long time (1 killing a year) for roughly a decade or more, or a high body count over the course of a few years (where they work with other accomplices).<br /> <br /> The Slasher book gives excellent examples of turning the regular serial killer into a truly great slasher, one that is sympathetic in ways and aided unwittingly by supernatural agency. They aren't meant to be persistent threats if sole agents, but go through periods of inactivity that really helps tell the other players, &quot;he's baaaack.&quot; If a ST were wise she'd recognize that this character has almost no Integrity and would be a failed roll away from the player losing control of his slasher character. <br /> <br /> That said, throw in a number of sympathies (only targets a particular type of predatory person), maybe a mentor who groomed your killer to take on an unrealized ideal, and give them a touch of the supernatural to separate him from your cookie cutter serial killer the next block over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","user":"TriCitiesLodge","date":".  Juvenile killer history is the exception here. 01-19-2018, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:25:14-08:00","id":1177386,"title":"","content":"Most Slashers are hardly &quot;Sane&quot; by any measurement, and he lacks some of the obvious quirks that fit into many of the Slasher profiles. I'd say Charmer or Genius fits best. Geniuses like to kill in unique, inventive, elaborate ways (though generally prefer complicated traps SAW style), which seems to fit your character. They are also good at reading people (helping them avoid getting caught), and generally hate it when their plans fall apart. They love reading their target and tailoring their strategy to them, which Austin here seems to like too. Typically clever, careful, and enjoy using a variety of skills for murder. They are a bit crazier then Austin seems to be (at most, Slashers can &quot;pretend&quot; to be normal person sane). I think you could fit him into this class if you really wanted to.<br /> <br /> There is always &quot;Mundane Serial Killer&quot; if you don't want to make him a slasher (or never get the books). &quot;Magical&quot; serial killers don't prevent normal ones from existing, and it lets you use the good old fashioned &quot;The real monster is MAN!&quot; cliche. He could also start out as a borderline slasher, transforming later in the story as a sort of power-boost (in return for sanity loss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}